schema: test/v2
level: epic
epic: E-PAGES
branch: HEAD
tests:
  unit: { count: 85, covers: "site.rs: the markdown subset renders bullets, paragraphs, code, bold and links and refuses every other construct by name; the release is refused when draft, pre-release, missing an Os::bundles kind x arch, carrying two files for one row or newer than the tree; every output check is red on a crafted file set (unresolved link or #id, a foreign absolute href, a changed CSP, an external src/srcset/url()/@import, script/iframe/form markup, an inline handler, a second script, site.js over 4096 bytes or naming a network or storage API, a denied name, download rows off by a kind or a tag, a token pair under 4.5:1 in either theme or token scope, motion outside reduced-motion); the PNG re-encode keeps pixels; BASE_URL is the github.io address of links.rs SOURCE_CODE. package.rs: HOMEPAGE is site::BASE_URL and a member or the tauri bundle left on the repo URL is drift. site.test.mjs: 14 navigator fixtures ask for the right dl-* block, show() fills both buttons, unhides #one and #pick, closes #all as Other systems; unknown leaves the page as without script" }
  integration: { count: 24, covers: "site.rs: the committed v0.1.0 release fixture builds exactly the site/ frame minus its tests plus site::ASSETS into a temp dir with no problem, links all 11 installer ids at releases/download/v0.1.0/, every shipped PNG decodes to its source's pixels, the page hides #one and #pick and keeps details#all open; the fixture minus the arm64 msi, a draft or a pre-release is refused and writes nothing; a non-empty --out is refused; node --test site/site.test.mjs is green; the built site's canonical address is package::HOMEPAGE and the tree's metadata drift is empty. pages_workflow.rs: pages.yml triggers only on push to main, release published (pre-release skipped) and dispatch; contents: read, pages and id-token write on deploy only; every action pinned by SHA, checkout and toolchain equal to release.yml; no persisted credentials or secret; the build reads releases/latest and uploads target/site only; one deploy at a time, never cancelled; timeouts and no continue-on-error" }
  e2e: { waived: "the epic's e2e is the live Pages deploy: it needs the owner's settings (Pages source = GitHub Actions, the github-pages v* tag rule) and the public network, and runs only when the epic merges to main (epic plan, E2E test plan); checked by the owner after the merge (gh run list --workflow pages.yml -L 1, curl -sI the address answers 200, DevTools Network shows one origin). Before it: the built site was served locally and rendered in headless Chrome at 1440 and 390 px, light and dark, script on and off (W3 result), and both pages.yml run steps were run by hand against the real latest release (W4)" }
